{"title":"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In preparation for the family's upcoming vacation, Tony puts together five bags of jelly beans, one bag for each day of the trip, with an equal number of jelly beans in each bag. \nTony then pours all the jelly beans out of the five bags and begins making patterns with them. One of the patterns that he makes has one jelly bean in a top row, three jelly \nbeans in the next row, five jelly beans in the row after that, and so on:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/8/5d8d992aae06c76627660a94e84799339d0031fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{ccccccccc}&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;*&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;\\\\&amp;&amp;&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;&amp;&amp;\\\\&amp;&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;&amp;\\\\&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;\\\\ *&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*&amp;*\\\\&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;\\vdots&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;\\end{array}\\]\" width=\"212\" height=\"122\" />\n</p><p>Continuing in this way, Tony finishes a row with none left over. For instance, if Tony had exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> jelly beans, he could finish the fifth row above with no jelly beans left over. However, when Tony finishes, there are between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> rows. Tony then scoops all the jelly beans and puts them all back into the five bags so that each bag once again contains the same number. How many jelly beans are in each bag? (Assume that no jelly bean gets put inside more than one bag.) \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the first row has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> jellybean and the second row has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> jellybeans, so the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/5/3657b37b69a5e1029f9182897c6b5dc7492cc1bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^\\text{th}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> row has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/3/03310b04b7e4f9e8976579b6d6477aa811e7cfa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2(n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> jellybeans.  That means the total number of jellybeans is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b641b323fd575f92b8f94e1a9117d3cbfce2c9de.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot n(1+2(n-1)+1)\\]\" width=\"175\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b2646c7468775c226c99c897854c52549d493a6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot n(2 + 2n - 2)\\]\" width=\"130\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e5967e472d53ac6463f6b04ffcba803a4de9a9f8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^2\\]\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />\nSince Tony finishes with more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> but less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> rows, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/c/d6cf1c5f5b70a5b9b8f675936999d0c036adfc6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 &lt; n &lt; 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"95\" height=\"13\" />.  He was able to evenly divide the jellybeans into five bags, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> is a muliple of five.  The only value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfies the conditions is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so each bag has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/6/056630bef321057e456fa13a64b66d1fac73387b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{225}{5} = \\boxed{45}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"78\" height=\"24\" /> jellybeans.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest\" title=\"2008 iTest\">2008 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems\">(Problems)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 iTest Pro